From e0565626fef409e1013294f2ee618950a30ea635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:25:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmre-kit: span fast path, SDF outline shapes, optional
 uxi/html

Interactive surfaces redraw large solid areas every frame; the kit spent
an SDF evaluation per pixel on them. Measured natively on a 1024x768
u32 surface:

  solid 600x470 rect           4.36 ms -> 0.125 ms
  full-screen rect             11.8 ms -> 0.165 ms
  1 px rounded window border   10.7 ms (path stroke) -> 0.123 ms
  soft shadow 600x470           4.8 ms -> 2.4 ms

- raster: for pure translations, each row's fully covered run is found
  analytically (rect, rounded rect, circle; conservative epsilon) and
  passed to Surface::fill_span; only edge pixels evaluate the SDF.
  Output is bit-identical to the per-pixel path (new equivalence test
  over shapes x paints x positions x soft).
- Surface::fill_span with a per-pixel default, bulk overrides for
  Framebuffer and BandView.
- Shape::RoundedRectOutline and Shape::CircleOutline: borders as SDF
  bands inside the edge; the hollow middle of each row is skipped.
- Features `uxi` (ux + layout) and `html` (implies uxi), on by default,
  so a draw-command renderer can leave the front ends out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
