index 707b2c0..32faa00 100644
--- a/ENGINE-INTEGRATION.md
+++ b/ENGINE-INTEGRATION.md
@@ -74,6 +74,20 @@ modules (`post`, `bloom_sweep`, `fair_queue`) are `std`-only; shapes, paths, gra
 text, layout and HTML all work unchanged, rendering into any `Surface` you implement.
 Atom OS uses this mode for its desktop.
 
+The `uxi` (intent tree + layout) and `html` features are also on by default. An app that
+drives the kit with draw commands directly can turn them off with the rest:
+`default-features = false` (add `features = ["uxi"]` or `["html"]` to keep them).
+
+### Fast paths for interactive surfaces
+
+For shapes placed by a pure translation, `raster::scan_convert` computes each row's fully
+covered run analytically and hands it to `Surface::fill_span` in one call; only pixels
+near the edges evaluate the SDF. The default `fill_span` blends pixel by pixel, so output
+is identical; a surface that overrides it with a bulk write (as `Framebuffer` does) makes
+large fills roughly as cheap as a memory fill. `Shape::RoundedRectOutline` and
+`Shape::CircleOutline` draw borders as SDF bands and skip the hollow middle, which is far
+cheaper than stroking a path for a 1 px window or button border.
+
 ## 3. Render a first frame
 
 The UXI path is the shortest route to a laid-out 2D interface:
